<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63689" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοβ-ός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lobe of the ear</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰτρητοι</span> (for wearing ear-rings) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.182
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				6.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				492a16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκροι λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					1401
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>lobe of the liver</i>, to which special attention was paid in
			divination, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				495
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				827
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				71c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Euphro
				7
			</span></i>: generally, <i>liver</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				159
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>lobe</i> of the lung, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				6.4
			</span></i>, al.; of the whole <i>lung</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Loc.Hom.</u>
				14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>capsule</i> or <i>pod</i> of leguminous plants (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλλοβος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				1.11.2
			</span></i>, etc.; esp. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φασίολοι</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλιχοι</span>, because they were
			eaten pod and all, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.557
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				5.175c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in rose
			leaves, <i>the white part</i>, elsewh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνυξ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.748
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
